        "Apply Pythagoras: $r^2 = 15^2 - h^2 = 225 - h^2$.",
        "Substitute $r^2$ into $V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "In the right-angled cross-section of the cone, apply Pythagoras' theorem with slant height $15\\text{ cm}$ and vertical height $h\\text{ cm}$:\n$$r^2 + h^2 = 15^2 \\implies r^2 = 225 - h^2$$",
        "Substitute $r^2$ into the cone volume formula:\n$$V = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(225 - h^2)h = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(225h - h^3)$$"
