      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate the volume function with respect to $h$:\n$$\\frac{dV}{dh} = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(225 - 3h^2) = \\pi(75 - h^2)$$",
        "Set $\\frac{dV}{dh} = 0$ to locate stationary values:\n$$\\pi(75 - h^2) = 0 \\implies h^2 = 75 \\implies h = \\sqrt{75} = 5\\sqrt{3} \\approx 8.66\\text{ cm} \\quad (\\text{since } h > 0)$$",
        "Determine the nature using the second derivative:\n$$\\frac{d^2V}{dh^2} = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi(-6h) = -2\\pi h$$\n$$\\text{At } h = 5\\sqrt{3}: \\quad \\frac{d^2V}{dh^2} = -10\\sqrt{3}\\pi < 0$$\nSince $\\frac{d^2V}{dh^2} < 0$, the volume is a **local maximum**."
